# The relay's own settings when it runs on the same machine as the server (docs/relay.md). Copy to relay.env.
# The relay reads the server's .env first and this file second, so the model settings both need (SPINE_LLM_MODEL, SPINE_LLM_MODELS,
# SPINE_EMBEDDINGS ...) and SPINE_RELAY_SECRET are written once, in .env. What only the relay may hold goes here: the provider's credential.
# The server never reads this file. The relay is not given SESSION_SECRET or BREVO_API_KEY (compose.yaml, systemd/spine-relay.service).

# The provider the relay calls: anthropic (default) or vertex
SPINE_LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Vertex AI in the EU instead (docs/deployment-gcp.md): stated, never defaulted, since residency is the endpoint. Authenticate
# with a service account (ADC); the relay refuses to start if GOOGLE_API_KEY or GEMINI_API_KEY is set (SECURITY.md M-8). The same
# credentials serve the embeddings when .env sets SPINE_EMBEDDINGS=vertex.
# SPINE_LLM_PROVIDER=vertex
# SPINE_LLM_ENDPOINT=aiplatform.eu.rep.googleapis.com
# SPINE_LLM_REGION=eu
# SPINE_LLM_PROJECT=your-gcp-project
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/etc/spine/vertex-sa.json

# Calls one account, one share link, one demo visitor and all demo visitors together may make a day (500, 200, 40, 400).
# For an account and a share link 0 or a bad value gives the default, not unlimited: set a large number instead. For the demo 0 means none.
# SPINE_RELAY_DAILY_CALLS=500
# SPINE_RELAY_SHARE_DAILY_CALLS=200
# SPINE_RELAY_DEMO_DAILY_CALLS=40
# SPINE_RELAY_DEMO_TOTAL_DAILY_CALLS=400
